	(text "Gain is set to target +4dBu (maximum)\nobviously this does not make it a pro-line-level device that way..\nwe'd need to probably have a certain amount of headroom.\nIf, instead we look at this as a -10dBV device, then we have\n~14dB of headroom with these values.\n\nGin=0.814 (Rin=10k, Rfb=16k)\nGout=1.228 (Rin=10k, Rfb=24k)\n\nAlternatively we can go closer to the PCM3060's \"2Vrms\" reference and just do:\nGin=0.5, Gout=2 :shrug:\n\nFor now, I've implemented the left channel of audio with less atten/gain."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
